WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.783 --> 00:00:03.050
[Cheering, Chattering]

2
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.244
[Indistinct]

3
00:00:23.705 --> 00:00:27.544
[Splash, Cheers]

4
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.595
Visualizing?

5
00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:41.043
All right.
You're up, tiger.

6
00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:44.211
You feel all right?
You look a little pale.

7
00:00:44.287 --> 00:00:47.192
I'm fine.
Does your neck still hurt?

8
00:00:47.261 --> 00:00:50.997
It'll be fine.
Maybe you should
do the two-and-a-half instead.

9
00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.906
I'm gonna do the three.
Well, it's better to nail
the two-and-a-half than-

10
00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:57.417
I'm gonna nail the three.

11
00:00:57.485 --> 00:00:59.421
All right.

12
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:04.058
Well, let's show these senior citizens
what a well-coached
12-year-old can do, huh?

13
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:24.912
[Man On P.A.]
Next diver, two-time National
Junior champion, Mary Carroll.

14
00:01:43.863 --> 00:01:45.492
[Exhales]

15
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.503
Damn it.

16
00:01:47.572 --> 00:01:52.038
You can do this.
Come on, just... see it. See it.

17
00:02:03.911 --> 00:02:09.288
[Sighs]
Big jump. Pike out. Rip it.

18
00:02:22.656 --> 00:02:26.027
[Silence]

19
00:02:35.487 --> 00:02:37.794
Call 911.
We need an ambulance.

20
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.110
[Mechanical Whirring]

21
00:03:30.044 --> 00:03:32.720
[Knocking]

22
00:03:34.112 --> 00:03:37.465
[Knocking Continues]

23
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.561
- I saw the light on.
- It's daytime.

24
00:03:49.638 --> 00:03:51.662
It's a figure of speech.

25
00:03:51.741 --> 00:03:53.731
Always so literal.

26
00:03:57.049 --> 00:04:00.816
- Got a new cane.
- Yeah.

27
00:04:00.888 --> 00:04:03.254
Guy in the store
said it was slimming.

28
00:04:03.324 --> 00:04:06.020
Vertical stripe.

29
00:04:06.094 --> 00:04:09.154
- Why are you here?
- Vogler is dead.

30
00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.133
What? What happened?

31
00:04:11.201 --> 00:04:15.194
Again with the literal translation.
Vogler, the idea.

32
00:04:15.274 --> 00:04:18.210
Mr. Destructo, Mr. Moneybags.
"Bow down before me."

33
00:04:18.278 --> 00:04:20.212
He is gone from the hospital.

34
00:04:20.281 --> 00:04:22.181
So things can go back
to the way they were.

35
00:04:22.251 --> 00:04:24.515
The way they were
was kind of weird.

36
00:04:24.587 --> 00:04:28.217
Hmm. Weird works for me.

37
00:04:28.292 --> 00:04:31.523
What are you saying?
Literally.

38
00:04:31.597 --> 00:04:35.534
- I want you to come back.
- Why?

39
00:04:35.602 --> 00:04:37.536
[Pager Beeps]

40
00:04:39.575 --> 00:04:41.440
[Beeping Continues]

41
00:04:41.511 --> 00:04:43.672
Please unclench.

42
00:04:43.747 --> 00:04:47.148
You're not on the clock,
and when you do that,
I clench and it's a whole thing.

43
00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.517
[Beeping Continues]
Could you look at your pager?

44
00:04:52.159 --> 00:04:54.251
[Beeping Stops]

45
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:59.063
It's no big deal.
Some sort of epidemic.
Not my area.

46
00:04:59.135 --> 00:05:01.933
- You should go. It's important.
- What I'm doing now is important.

47
00:05:02.005 --> 00:05:06.203
- Why do you want me back?
- 'Cause you're a good doctor.

48
00:05:08.582 --> 00:05:12.074
- That's it?
- That's not enough?

49
00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:14.955
Not for me.

50
00:05:18.829 --> 00:05:20.763
Go deal with your plague.

51
00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:31.943
[People Chattering]
[Woman On P.A.]
You are in a quarantined area.

52
00:05:32.014 --> 00:05:36.577
Please remain calm and stay in line.
A doctor will see you shortly.

53
00:05:36.654 --> 00:05:41.092
When you see a doctor,
you will receive a blue or yellow form.

54
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.063
Patients with blue forms
must immediately exit
to the parking lot.

55
00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.624
Dr. House. Need you here.

56
00:05:47.702 --> 00:05:51.571
Sorry. Lot of sick people.
I might catch something.

57
00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:53.576
Ajudge at the campus pool center
collapsed.

58
00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:55.977
L.P. Revealed a virulent form
of bacterial meningitis.

59
00:05:56.048 --> 00:05:58.539
Great. You got it diagnosed.
You don't need me.

60
00:05:58.617 --> 00:06:02.281
2,500 people at the pool center
were exposed.

61
00:06:02.356 --> 00:06:04.290
They're being bused
to all the neighboring hospitals.

62
00:06:04.359 --> 00:06:06.554
That's a problem with resources,
not diagnostics.

63
00:06:06.629 --> 00:06:09.223
L- I'd be completely lost,
get in everyone's way.

64
00:06:09.298 --> 00:06:12.529
Joe. Dr. House doesn't have
a blue slip.

65
00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:15.472
No one leaves the quarantine area
without a blue slip.

66
00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.443
You are a doctor at this hospital.
Act like one.

67
00:06:18.512 --> 00:06:20.446
And...

68
00:06:20.515 --> 00:06:22.641
take these.

69
00:06:22.718 --> 00:06:25.812
[Man Coughing]

70
00:06:31.329 --> 00:06:33.854
102.

71
00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:36.425
You win a trip
to the second floor.

72
00:06:36.503 --> 00:06:38.493
Next.

73
00:06:42.078 --> 00:06:45.845
All right.
No fever. No rash.

74
00:06:45.918 --> 00:06:49.376
You're fine.
Take these two pills.

75
00:06:49.456 --> 00:06:52.721
And show this blue slip
to Security on your way out.

76
00:06:52.793 --> 00:06:54.351
Next.

77
00:06:54.428 --> 00:06:56.259
Take these. Go home.

78
00:06:56.331 --> 00:06:59.027
Talk to your daughter.
What?

79
00:06:59.102 --> 00:07:04.598
Your pants, your blouse, your scarf
are all freshly dry cleaned.
Everything except your jacket.

80
00:07:04.677 --> 00:07:07.840
It's got a smudge on it.
Probably two days old.

81
00:07:07.914 --> 00:07:09.848
Which means you didn't know
the jacket had been worn.

82
00:07:09.917 --> 00:07:12.887
So either your husband is a cross-dresser,

83
00:07:12.954 --> 00:07:16.082
or your daughter's been
borrowing your clothes
without telling you.

84
00:07:16.159 --> 00:07:18.389
She probably wants to look older
to get into bars.

85
00:07:18.462 --> 00:07:21.454
I don't have a daughter.

86
00:07:26.173 --> 00:07:28.869
Next.

87
00:07:28.943 --> 00:07:31.605
So I have it?
Take the yellow form
to the second floor.

88
00:07:31.681 --> 00:07:33.615
You're gonna be fine.
I'm gonna die.

89
00:07:33.683 --> 00:07:37.279
It's treatable-
as long as you go to the second floor.

90
00:07:37.355 --> 00:07:39.289
Next.

91
00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.722
[Sighs]
Yow.

92
00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:45.923
Fever?
Does that mean I have it?

93
00:07:46.001 --> 00:07:48.469
Do you have a rash?

94
00:07:48.538 --> 00:07:50.506
Come on.

95
00:07:51.975 --> 00:07:54.101
It's from my new bathing suit.
I've had it a week.

96
00:07:54.179 --> 00:07:56.237
Yeah.

97
00:07:56.315 --> 00:07:59.148
Does your neck hurt?
If it does, you hit the trifecta.

98
00:07:59.219 --> 00:08:01.915
It's nothing.
I pulled it trying to do
a three-and-a-half tuck.

99
00:08:01.989 --> 00:08:05.015
Where are your parents?
We live in Chicago.

100
00:08:05.093 --> 00:08:07.288
I'm here with my coach.

101
00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.431
I wanted to see
what you were writing.

102
00:08:16.343 --> 00:08:18.367
Go like this.

103
00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.314
Ow.

104
00:08:23.085 --> 00:08:24.814
Go like this.

105
00:08:30.363 --> 00:08:32.797
Take these pills.

106
00:08:32.866 --> 00:08:35.096
Blue slip will
get you out of here.

107
00:08:37.038 --> 00:08:39.302
Next.

108
00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:41.741
You're coming with me.

109
00:08:41.812 --> 00:08:45.544
[Woman On P.A.]
Proceed to the second floor
for further examination.

110
00:08:45.617 --> 00:08:48.085
You're gonna need a C.T. Scan.
Second floor.

111
00:08:48.153 --> 00:08:50.087
Take the elevators,
follow the parade.

112
00:08:50.156 --> 00:08:52.317
Next.
[Whistles]

113
00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.365
[Chase]
Maybe it's something systemic.
[Foreman] Or maybe it's meningitis.

114
00:09:00.437 --> 00:09:03.600
She's had the rash a week.
If it was this meningitis
she'd be dead by now.

115
00:09:03.675 --> 00:09:05.609
You guys figure
we're done down there?

116
00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:08.442
The 800 people milling around
are just waiting for the bathroom?

117
00:09:08.515 --> 00:09:12.247
Twelve-year-old female.
Fever, rash, neck pains.
Not meningitis.

118
00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.254
It's the definition
of meningitis.

119
00:09:14.323 --> 00:09:17.622
Sure. Pus in the spinal canal
makes it hurt to move your head
up and down,

120
00:09:17.695 --> 00:09:19.526
but her neck only hurts
moving side to side.

121
00:09:19.597 --> 00:09:21.792
- Oh, side to side.
- Doesn't fit.

122
00:09:21.868 --> 00:09:24.462
The three of you, lobby, now.

123
00:09:24.537 --> 00:09:26.629
Those little pills you're passing out
so efficiently...

124
00:09:26.707 --> 00:09:28.765
aren't gonna do
Miss Louganis squat.

125
00:09:28.843 --> 00:09:30.811
You just don't want to deal
with the epidemic.

126
00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.814
That's right.
I'm subjecting a 12-year-old...

127
00:09:32.883 --> 00:09:36.250
to a battery of dangerous
and invasive tests
to avoid being bored.

128
00:09:38.156 --> 00:09:40.989
Okay, maybe I would do that.
But I'm not.

129
00:09:41.061 --> 00:09:43.222
If it turns out
she's got meningitis,

130
00:09:43.296 --> 00:09:46.026
you're right, you win;
but if we go back downstairs
and she dies-

131
00:09:46.101 --> 00:09:48.899
[Vibrates Lips]
Your face will be so red.

132
00:09:50.373 --> 00:09:52.307
You have one hour.

133
00:09:54.179 --> 00:09:58.139
Get a lumbar puncture.
Some brain infections can be
pretty clever at hide-and-seek.

134
00:09:58.217 --> 00:10:00.811
I'll get on her blood work.
No, you won't.

135
00:10:00.888 --> 00:10:04.187
You, sir, will research all the causes
in the universe of neck pain.

136
00:10:04.259 --> 00:10:07.923
- The list is, like, two miles long.
- Start with the letter "A."

137
00:10:07.998 --> 00:10:11.024
And put her on rifampin.
Rifampin is for meningitis.
You just said-

138
00:10:11.102 --> 00:10:13.036
In case I'm wrong.

139
00:10:13.105 --> 00:10:14.868
It has happened.

140
00:10:17.244 --> 00:10:20.645
[Man Coughing]

141
00:10:21.851 --> 00:10:24.149
[Coughing]

142
00:10:30.797 --> 00:10:33.391
Brenda, I need a C.B.C. Chem 7
in 2046.

143
00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:36.630
Hold on.
Excuse me. Excuse me.

144
00:10:36.705 --> 00:10:38.831
Hey, there's a line here.
That's why I said excuse me.

145
00:10:38.907 --> 00:10:41.239
Brenda, I need a bed and a-
We all need stuff.

146
00:10:41.311 --> 00:10:43.335
Push me again.

147
00:10:43.415 --> 00:10:45.246
Brenda, I need a bed and a nurse
for a lumbar puncture.

148
00:10:45.316 --> 00:10:48.012
No beds, no nurses for at least four hours.
I've only got one.

149
00:10:48.087 --> 00:10:50.521
Your patient only has an hour to live
unless she gets a lumbar puncture?

150
00:10:50.591 --> 00:10:53.992
Cuddy only gave us an hour
to work on the patient.

151
00:10:54.062 --> 00:10:56.860
- Back of the line.
- [Snickering]

152
00:10:59.836 --> 00:11:03.932
[Woman On P.A.]
Do not leave the quarantine area
until you have been seen by a doctor.

153
00:11:04.009 --> 00:11:07.707
When you see a doctor,
you will receive a blue or yellow form-

154
00:11:07.781 --> 00:11:11.182
This novocaine will numb you
for the lumbar puncture.

155
00:11:11.252 --> 00:11:14.085
Sorry this has to be
so public, Mary.

156
00:11:14.156 --> 00:11:17.455
Normally I'm in a bathing suit
with 5,000 people staring at my butt.

157
00:11:17.528 --> 00:11:19.462
I can block this out.

158
00:11:20.466 --> 00:11:25.097
These kids are all very mature.
Travel around the country
from event to event.

159
00:11:27.375 --> 00:11:29.741
Okay, I want you to hold your knees
and tuck your head.

160
00:11:29.811 --> 00:11:32.041
- Like a dive?
- Exactly.

161
00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:38.247
Good. Great.
Don't forget to breathe.

162
00:11:40.626 --> 00:11:42.423
All right.

163
00:11:42.496 --> 00:11:44.464
[Clatter]
Sorry.

164
00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.698
Geez. Coach, help me out here.

165
00:11:47.769 --> 00:11:49.759
Play a little defense
before I poke the wrong thing.

166
00:11:54.746 --> 00:11:57.340
Okay, here we go.

167
00:11:57.416 --> 00:12:00.647
[Groans]

168
00:12:00.722 --> 00:12:04.920
- Ow. I feel it. Ow. I feel it. I fee- Ow.
- Try to relax, Mary. Try to relax.

169
00:12:04.995 --> 00:12:06.860
Relax.

170
00:12:15.142 --> 00:12:18.977
What letter are you up to?
"A."

171
00:12:19.047 --> 00:12:22.039
Torture combing through
all that stuff, ain't it?

172
00:12:22.118 --> 00:12:25.987
- Real dull. Awful.
- It's no problem.

173
00:12:26.057 --> 00:12:27.581
Well, thank goodness.

174
00:12:27.659 --> 00:12:31.323
A lot of people would resent
having to do this.

175
00:12:36.638 --> 00:12:41.076
[Woman On P.A.]
If you receive a blue form,
please exit the area.

176
00:12:41.145 --> 00:12:44.546
If you receive a yellow form,
please proceed to the second floor.

177
00:12:44.616 --> 00:12:46.550
Where's the 12-year-old girl
that was here?

178
00:12:46.619 --> 00:12:49.383
Needed the gurney.
She just had a lumbar puncture.

179
00:12:49.456 --> 00:12:52.152
She's not supposed to be moved.
Sorry. We needed the gurney.

180
00:13:01.105 --> 00:13:02.902
[Sighs]
Hey.

181
00:13:02.976 --> 00:13:05.501
- Hey.
- You okay? How's your head feeling?

182
00:13:05.578 --> 00:13:07.739
She's got a headache
and she's dizzy.

183
00:13:07.815 --> 00:13:10.375
She shouldn't have been moved
after the procedure.
I'm sorry.

184
00:13:11.353 --> 00:13:14.550
I'm fine.
What did the test show?

185
00:13:14.625 --> 00:13:16.683
No meningitis and no other infections.

186
00:13:16.761 --> 00:13:21.358
But you're not carrying a blue form.
I have something else, don't I?

187
00:13:21.433 --> 00:13:24.869
Something's causing your symptoms.
We're gonna keep you here
overnight.

188
00:13:24.939 --> 00:13:28.136
I know it's a little crazy in here,
but hopefully it'll settle down...

189
00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:31.008
and we'll be able
to get you a room.

190
00:13:32.148 --> 00:13:37.712
I'm sorry.
I'm not usually all emotional like this.
I just-

191
00:13:38.958 --> 00:13:42.588
You're doing great.
Your folks land in a few hours.

192
00:13:42.664 --> 00:13:44.756
I just- I haven't slept.
I'm so tired.

193
00:13:47.036 --> 00:13:49.561
Oh, my God. My eye's bleeding.

194
00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.234
What is it?
What's happening?

195
00:13:55.915 --> 00:13:58.577
Oh, don't worry.

196
00:13:58.652 --> 00:14:02.144
The antibiotic we gave you
in case you had meningitis
can turn your tears reddish.

197
00:14:02.223 --> 00:14:04.088
That's not blood.

198
00:14:12.938 --> 00:14:16.305
But that-

199
00:14:16.377 --> 00:14:18.311
That's blood.

200
00:14:24.522 --> 00:14:27.116
That's going into my stomach?

201
00:14:27.192 --> 00:14:29.456
The lavage showed blood
in your G.I. Tract.

202
00:14:29.529 --> 00:14:31.587
We need to find
where it's coming from.

203
00:14:31.665 --> 00:14:33.599
You won't feel it.

204
00:14:33.667 --> 00:14:37.536
I'm gonna numb the back of your throat,
and Dr. Foreman is gonna
give you a sedative. Open.

205
00:14:38.607 --> 00:14:41.269
- Ugh.
- Swallow.

206
00:14:41.345 --> 00:14:43.335
[Coughing]
Now lay on your side for me.

207
00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:49.048
And... here we go.

208
00:14:52.761 --> 00:14:56.128
- Yell fire or something.
- People, this area is highly contagious.

209
00:14:56.199 --> 00:14:59.396
Please step back. Highly contagious.

210
00:14:59.469 --> 00:15:04.635
[Scoffs]
All right. Try to relax, Mary.
This shouldn't take too long.

211
00:15:04.711 --> 00:15:08.203
- [Coughs]
- I don't see any tears or lesions.

212
00:15:11.553 --> 00:15:14.489
[Chase]
All right. I'm in the stomach.

213
00:15:14.557 --> 00:15:16.718
It's not bleeding.

214
00:15:16.795 --> 00:15:19.765
There was more than a tablespoon
of blood in the mouth,
so it's gotta be there.

215
00:15:19.832 --> 00:15:21.993
Maybe her small intestine.

216
00:15:22.068 --> 00:15:25.401
Thirty feet of digestive tract,
it could be anywhere in there.

217
00:15:25.473 --> 00:15:28.874
We're not gonna see it with this.

218
00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.841
Believe it or not, this is a camera.

219
00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:39.050
You swallow it,
and it goes all the way
through your system.

220
00:15:40.394 --> 00:15:43.693
The antennae pick up the signal
from the pill.

221
00:15:43.765 --> 00:15:46.233
Then we look at the video
of your intestines,

222
00:15:46.302 --> 00:15:49.066
see where the blood is coming from,
and fix it.

223
00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.234
All right? Water?

224
00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.244
Down the hatch.

225
00:16:04.795 --> 00:16:09.096
[House]
Think I've seen this movie.

226
00:16:09.167 --> 00:16:12.069
The ending's kind of dark.

227
00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:14.071
You want one?

228
00:16:15.877 --> 00:16:17.969
How come you did the endoscopy?

229
00:16:18.045 --> 00:16:20.309
- He asked for help.
- Her blood pressure was high.

230
00:16:20.382 --> 00:16:22.577
Foreman is not your boss.

231
00:16:22.653 --> 00:16:24.917
When I tell you to do something-

232
00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:26.924
Whoa. Hold it there.

233
00:16:26.992 --> 00:16:29.860
Back it up a couple of frames.

234
00:16:31.732 --> 00:16:34.634
Oh, yeah.
That's your money shot.

235
00:16:34.702 --> 00:16:36.636
I don't see anything.

236
00:16:36.705 --> 00:16:41.143
Really? "Ginormous" thing
on the right side of her intestine.
That doesn't intrigue you?

237
00:16:41.212 --> 00:16:43.476
Does "ginormous" mean really big,
or really, really small?

238
00:16:43.549 --> 00:16:47.350
- 'Cause I don't see anything.
- There? The Dieulafoy?

239
00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.354
Well, we can burn off
the swollen blood vessel,

240
00:16:49.423 --> 00:16:52.620
but it still doesn't account
for her other symptoms.

241
00:16:52.695 --> 00:16:54.719
No, but it does tell us something.

242
00:16:54.798 --> 00:16:56.822
Though I have no idea what.

243
00:16:56.899 --> 00:16:59.993
Could be a precursor
to intestinal intussusception.

244
00:17:00.071 --> 00:17:04.337
Precursor isn't causing
all her other symptoms.
What else?

245
00:17:04.411 --> 00:17:07.574
You, in the lobby now.

246
00:17:07.649 --> 00:17:11.915
I hurt my leg. I have a note.
You had your hour-
three, actually.

247
00:17:11.988 --> 00:17:15.321
Dr. Chase, I told you to tell us
when our time was up.

248
00:17:16.428 --> 00:17:19.829
She has intestinal bleeding.
She'll wait.

249
00:17:19.899 --> 00:17:22.561
Two more buses just arrived.
We need you downstairs.

250
00:17:22.636 --> 00:17:26.596
No, you need more nurses,
but you cut back
on the nursing staff,

251
00:17:26.674 --> 00:17:29.040
so now you've got doctors doing
what nurses should be doing.

252
00:17:29.112 --> 00:17:31.046
That's true.

253
00:17:31.114 --> 00:17:35.950
I wonder if that has anything to do
with you costing us $100 million.

254
00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:43.627
[Woman On P.A.]
Attention. If you do not have a blue form,

255
00:17:43.698 --> 00:17:47.465
you will not be allowed
to leave the quarantine area.

256
00:17:47.537 --> 00:17:49.471
Go. Be free.

257
00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.405
If it's not the intussusception,
what about stomach cancer?

258
00:17:52.511 --> 00:17:54.445
[Wilson]
Does she have any abdominal pain?
[Chase] No.

259
00:17:54.514 --> 00:17:56.812
Then it's not stomach cancer.
Have you ruled out sepsis?

260
00:17:56.883 --> 00:18:01.149
The L.P. And blood smears
showed no signs of infection.
Here. Take these two pills and you can go.

261
00:18:01.223 --> 00:18:04.159
Well, the lab's working
at double their capacity.
Maybe someone screwed up.

262
00:18:04.228 --> 00:18:07.254
No fever, no neck pain.

263
00:18:07.332 --> 00:18:09.823
Take the elevator to the third floor-
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Wrong form.

264
00:18:09.902 --> 00:18:14.896
- No fever, no neck pain. She's fine.
- Smell her hair. No chlorine.

265
00:18:14.976 --> 00:18:18.468
Which means she wasn't at the pool,
which means she's come
to a quarantined area...

266
00:18:18.547 --> 00:18:21.483
because she's an idiot or she's insane.

267
00:18:21.551 --> 00:18:25.681
No one is that stupid.
East wing, psych ward. Bye-bye.

268
00:18:27.492 --> 00:18:29.960
Neck pain could be a symptom
for bone cancer.

269
00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:33.000
You up to the B's? Well done.

270
00:18:33.068 --> 00:18:36.526
That would account for all her
meningeal symptoms- rash, fever.

271
00:18:36.605 --> 00:18:38.266
You're fine.
Take these two pills.

272
00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.364
Get a sample of her bone marrow.

273
00:18:40.444 --> 00:18:42.502
From here?
Break time.

274
00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.947
- I need more than 15 minutes.
- Use Chase's break too.

275
00:18:47.955 --> 00:18:50.515
Go.

276
00:18:52.027 --> 00:18:55.828
You should just fire Chase.
What, and miss out
on all this fun?

277
00:18:55.899 --> 00:18:58.163
So you're gonna
torture him for a while
and then fire him?

278
00:18:58.235 --> 00:19:00.669
That's cold.
You don't think he has it coming?

279
00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:04.005
Hey, I said fire him.
That's cold.

280
00:19:04.077 --> 00:19:06.203
All he did was save his job.
What?

281
00:19:06.279 --> 00:19:08.679
He completely screwed you over.

282
00:19:08.751 --> 00:19:12.347
Right rudder.

283
00:19:12.422 --> 00:19:14.219
Bank, bank, bank.

284
00:19:14.291 --> 00:19:18.661
Good coffee?
The rest of this hospital
is busting its tail and you're-

285
00:19:18.731 --> 00:19:22.895
- What are you doing?
- Trying to think of anything except
the produce department at Whole Foods.

286
00:19:24.439 --> 00:19:29.104
I am working. It got hot.
Stop acting like a 13-year-old.
Sorry.

287
00:19:29.178 --> 00:19:32.046
You just don't usually see breasts like that
on deans of medicine.

288
00:19:32.115 --> 00:19:34.777
Oh, women can't be
heads ofhospitals?
Orjust ugly ones?

289
00:19:34.853 --> 00:19:39.085
No, they can be babes.
It's just you don't usually see their fun bags.

290
00:19:40.294 --> 00:19:44.197
Your 3:00 interview
for Dr. Cameron's position
is in your office.

291
00:19:44.266 --> 00:19:48.601
Not interviewing today.
I don't know if you've heard,
but there's this big-time epidemic.

292
00:19:48.673 --> 00:19:53.270
Many sick people.
Puking in the hallways. It's crazy.
We can reschedule.

293
00:19:53.345 --> 00:19:56.143
No, you won't.
You will interview this person.

294
00:19:56.216 --> 00:19:59.379
And ifhe can put
two sentences together,
you will send him to the lobby...

295
00:19:59.454 --> 00:20:01.388
where he will do his job.

296
00:20:01.456 --> 00:20:03.446
Unlike the two of you.

297
00:20:05.496 --> 00:20:10.059
Come on. You know I can't do
a bone marrow aspiration
in the hallway.

298
00:20:10.136 --> 00:20:12.070
And I can't give you
a procedure room.

299
00:20:12.138 --> 00:20:14.436
I just need something at least
close to a sterile environment.

300
00:20:14.509 --> 00:20:16.635
I need ten more nurses.

301
00:20:16.712 --> 00:20:19.272
Brenda, listen. Listen.
She'll die.

302
00:20:19.348 --> 00:20:23.183
At least she'll have a bed then.
Put that over there.

303
00:20:33.869 --> 00:20:36.133
[Mary]
Are there dead people
in those cabinets?

304
00:20:36.205 --> 00:20:39.470
[Chuckles]
I hope that's who's in there.

305
00:20:49.323 --> 00:20:51.985
Just be calm. Relax.

306
00:20:53.263 --> 00:20:55.857
[Groans]

307
00:20:57.167 --> 00:21:00.432
Ow. Ow, ow, ow, ow.

308
00:21:00.506 --> 00:21:02.872
Hang on.

309
00:21:02.942 --> 00:21:06.674
[Groaning]
Hang on.

310
00:21:12.022 --> 00:21:16.551
You know, I really admire the way
you don't care what anyone thinks.
You just do what you want, the way you want.

311
00:21:18.898 --> 00:21:20.832
So you went to Hopkins
for both undergrad
and med school?

312
00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:24.496
- That's right.
- He's in a band.

313
00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:29.338
- You're into music?
- Totally.

314
00:21:29.412 --> 00:21:31.380
What kind of music do you play?

315
00:21:31.448 --> 00:21:35.215
Mostly blues, you know,
James Cotton,
some original stuff.

316
00:21:35.288 --> 00:21:39.520
- Oh, dude, you are so hired.
- Really?

317
00:21:39.593 --> 00:21:43.586
- Not a chance.
- Why?

318
00:21:43.665 --> 00:21:46.259
Tattoo.

319
00:21:47.204 --> 00:21:51.608
Wow. I thought you'd be the last person
to have a problem with nonconformity.

320
00:21:51.676 --> 00:21:53.940
Nonconformity. Right.

321
00:21:54.014 --> 00:21:57.781
I can't remember the last time
I saw a 20-something kid with a tattoo
of an Asian letter on his wrist.

322
00:21:57.852 --> 00:21:59.820
You are one wicked freethinker.

323
00:21:59.888 --> 00:22:02.118
You want to be a rebel?
Stop being cool.

324
00:22:02.192 --> 00:22:05.252
Wear a pocket protector like he does,
and get a haircut,

325
00:22:05.329 --> 00:22:08.197
like the Asian kids who don't leave
the library for 20-hour stretches.

326
00:22:08.266 --> 00:22:10.256
They're the ones who don't care
what you think.

327
00:22:11.337 --> 00:22:14.329
Sayonara.

328
00:22:20.017 --> 00:22:23.647
So, should I go through all the resumes
looking for Asian names?

329
00:22:23.721 --> 00:22:28.421
Actually, the Asian kids are probably
just responding to parental pressure,
but my point is still valid.

330
00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:33.026
[Sighs]
So when do they think
you're getting out of here?

331
00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:35.034
They don't know.

332
00:22:35.103 --> 00:22:37.833
You don't look sick.
Better hope you're not.

333
00:22:37.908 --> 00:22:41.275
- This equipment looks
like it's 100 years old.
- Just got it out of storage.

334
00:22:41.346 --> 00:22:44.679
It is the previous generation,
but it works just fine.

335
00:22:44.751 --> 00:22:46.685
Could you, uh-
Could you guys give us a second?

336
00:22:48.356 --> 00:22:50.380
If it's good news, you can tell them.

337
00:22:50.459 --> 00:22:54.657
Okay. We're, uh, we're pretty sure
it's not cancer.

338
00:22:54.732 --> 00:22:56.962
- Hey, that's great.
- I'll call your parents.

339
00:22:57.034 --> 00:23:00.664
Well, we still can't release her.
We still don't know yet exactly
what's causing the-

340
00:23:00.740 --> 00:23:02.730
[Monitor Beeping]

341
00:23:04.945 --> 00:23:07.413
Mary?

342
00:23:07.482 --> 00:23:11.419
- What's wrong?
- She's having an absence seizure.
Mary? You okay?

343
00:23:11.488 --> 00:23:16.256
She looks fine.
I need some help over here.
Push two milligrams Ativan, stat.

344
00:23:16.328 --> 00:23:19.729
[Beeping Continues]

345
00:23:33.419 --> 00:23:35.683
[Water Running]

346
00:23:35.754 --> 00:23:37.915
Are you sure it was
an absence seizure?

347
00:23:37.991 --> 00:23:40.083
Absolutely.
She was totally unresponsive...

348
00:23:40.161 --> 00:23:42.755
and unaware of what was
going on around her.

349
00:23:43.966 --> 00:23:45.900
[Grunting]

350
00:23:45.969 --> 00:23:47.903
Do you mind?
We're trying to work.

351
00:23:47.972 --> 00:23:50.270
We should get back out there.
Cuddy's gonna be looking for us.

352
00:23:50.342 --> 00:23:52.902
Looking, but not finding.
Did you do an E.E.G.?

353
00:23:52.979 --> 00:23:56.643
Seizure frequency's increasing.
They-They're almost constant now.
Five in the last half hour.

354
00:23:56.717 --> 00:23:58.582
Which tells us-
It's definitely in her brain.

355
00:23:58.653 --> 00:24:01.121
- And it's getting worse.
- And?

356
00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:03.248
[Grunting Continues]

357
00:24:03.326 --> 00:24:06.022
Good Lord.
Are you having a bowl movement
or a baby?

358
00:24:06.097 --> 00:24:09.555
- [Chase]
Could be barbiturate withdrawal.
- No, it can't be drugs.

359
00:24:09.635 --> 00:24:13.436
She's tested at every meet she competes at.
A bleed in the brain
could cause seizures.

360
00:24:13.508 --> 00:24:15.634
Rat poison?
Could also cause the neck pain.

361
00:24:15.710 --> 00:24:18.178
You think she's eating off the floor
of her folks' garage?

362
00:24:18.247 --> 00:24:20.181
Doesn't have to be.

363
00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.548
Who would poison a 12-year-old?

364
00:24:22.619 --> 00:24:27.250
Well, let's see now.
There's the 18-year-old has-been that she
beat out to make the Nationals,

365
00:24:27.327 --> 00:24:31.264
the has-been's parents, jealous siblings,
sociopathic swim fan,

366
00:24:31.333 --> 00:24:35.031
and then there's just your plain old
garden variety whack job.

367
00:24:35.104 --> 00:24:37.072
[Toilet Flushes]

368
00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:42.977
Hey.

369
00:24:43.049 --> 00:24:47.247
- You know what a hemorrhoid is?
- No.

370
00:24:47.322 --> 00:24:51.486
Well, Google it.
And try some raisin bran
instead of the doughnuts.

371
00:24:54.899 --> 00:24:57.163
Do a C.T. Scan.
Check for intracranial bleeding.

372
00:24:57.236 --> 00:24:59.796
Not a chance.
Radiology's totally swamped.

373
00:24:59.871 --> 00:25:02.841
If our patient's bleeding into her brain,
she's gonna be dead in eight hours.

374
00:25:02.910 --> 00:25:06.209
She could be, but a meningitis patient
will be without a C.T. Scan.

375
00:25:07.216 --> 00:25:11.779
- When I was in med school,
I had this old professor-
- Who touched you in the naughty place?

376
00:25:13.024 --> 00:25:17.792
Before the C.T. Scan was introduced,
he specialized in transcranial ultrasound.

377
00:25:17.864 --> 00:25:19.798
Hmm.

378
00:25:19.866 --> 00:25:22.664
Ancient, but if there's
enough bleeding it might work.

379
00:25:22.737 --> 00:25:26.469
Okay, do what the guy
who didn't specialize
in neurology said.

380
00:25:26.542 --> 00:25:29.010
It was my idea.

381
00:25:29.079 --> 00:25:32.207
Nyah, nyah, nyah.
You've still gotta cover "Q" to "Z."

382
00:25:42.398 --> 00:25:45.492
Sorry I'm late.
I was taking a dump.

383
00:25:46.604 --> 00:25:49.869
I'm guessing I'm better off
interviewing right after
than right before.

384
00:25:51.310 --> 00:25:53.334
Dr. Petra Gilmar, Dr. Gregory House.

385
00:25:53.413 --> 00:25:59.183
You actually speak four languages,
or are you just banking on never
being interviewed by anyone who does?

386
00:25:59.254 --> 00:26:02.122
It's true, and I can swear
in two more.

387
00:26:03.193 --> 00:26:05.127
Why are you leaving Dr. Hazel?

388
00:26:05.196 --> 00:26:09.133
Did you fall for him and can't handle it,
or was it the other way around?

389
00:26:09.201 --> 00:26:12.568
- Yes, well, pretty much
every fellowship ends that way.
- No, it was nothing like that.

390
00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:14.698
- You Jewish?
- Yes.

391
00:26:14.776 --> 00:26:17.267
- Is it true what they say aboutJewish foreplay?
- [Stammering]

392
00:26:17.347 --> 00:26:18.974
- Two hours of begging?
- I heard four.

393
00:26:19.048 --> 00:26:21.106
Well, actually, I'm only halfJewish.

394
00:26:24.457 --> 00:26:26.982
Look, I know you like
to play games with people.

395
00:26:27.059 --> 00:26:30.051
I know you like
to say outrageous things
and study how they react.

396
00:26:30.131 --> 00:26:32.929
What you should know about me
is that I grew up with four brothers.

397
00:26:33.001 --> 00:26:36.733
Keep your hands to yourself,
I'm okay with anything
that comes out of your mouth.

398
00:26:38.809 --> 00:26:42.336
Uh, well, that's, uh, great.
I think that's all we need.

399
00:26:42.415 --> 00:26:45.646
Thank you for coming by.
Thank you.

400
00:26:58.103 --> 00:27:02.438
- That's our Hitler!
- No way.

401
00:27:02.510 --> 00:27:05.502
Are you kidding?
Her background's perfect.

402
00:27:05.580 --> 00:27:07.480
She's smart, she can obviously deal
with your insanity-

403
00:27:07.550 --> 00:27:09.540
You see her shoes?
Her shoes?

404
00:27:09.619 --> 00:27:12.611
What, did your horoscope in Vogue
tell you to avoid women wearing green shoes?

405
00:27:12.689 --> 00:27:15.214
The eyes can mislead,
a smile can lie,

406
00:27:15.294 --> 00:27:17.558
but the shoes always tell the truth.

407
00:27:17.630 --> 00:27:20.895
- They were Prada.
Means she has good taste.
- They were not Prada.

408
00:27:20.968 --> 00:27:23.493
You wouldn't know Prada
if one stepped on your scrotum.

409
00:27:23.571 --> 00:27:27.201
Okay. Well, they were nice. Pointy.
Exactly.

410
00:27:27.277 --> 00:27:29.837
They were stylish,
and very painful to wear.

411
00:27:29.914 --> 00:27:31.904
Only an incredibly shallow,
insecure woman...

412
00:27:31.983 --> 00:27:35.419
would rather be in pain all day long
than wear a decent-looking,
comfortable shoe,

413
00:27:35.488 --> 00:27:37.422
and that's exactly the type
I don't need around here.

414
00:27:37.491 --> 00:27:39.425
No. Someone
who can handle a lot of pain...

415
00:27:39.494 --> 00:27:42.486
is exactly the type you do need.

416
00:27:58.587 --> 00:28:00.418
Excuse me.

417
00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.798
What are you doing?

418
00:28:57.870 --> 00:29:00.236
I'm "ultrasounding" your head.

419
00:29:00.307 --> 00:29:04.300
You're still having seizures.
This should help us
figure out what's going on.

420
00:29:08.318 --> 00:29:11.810
Blue form to the security guard.
You're not gonna be happy
with anyone.

421
00:29:11.890 --> 00:29:14.256
So what, your advice is...

422
00:29:14.326 --> 00:29:17.124
hire someone I'm not happy with
and be happy?

423
00:29:17.196 --> 00:29:19.164
No, my advice is much more subtle.
Stop being an ass.

424
00:29:19.232 --> 00:29:22.862
You always find some tiny little flaw
to push people away.

425
00:29:22.937 --> 00:29:25.805
Oh, now it's people.
I thought we were talking
about fellowship applicants.

426
00:29:25.875 --> 00:29:28.503
You have a history of this.
Well, when I do decide...

427
00:29:28.579 --> 00:29:32.539
to push you away, I hope there's
a small person kneeling behind you,
so you fall down and hurt your head.

428
00:29:32.619 --> 00:29:35.521
Take these.
There's water over there.
Blue form to the guard.

429
00:29:35.589 --> 00:29:37.523
And you're done.

430
00:29:37.592 --> 00:29:41.688
You had the perfect person,
and you blew it.

431
00:29:41.764 --> 00:29:43.698
You saw the shoes.

432
00:29:43.767 --> 00:29:47.134
I'm not talking about her.
You're talking about Cameron.

433
00:29:47.205 --> 00:29:49.639
I'm talking about every woman
you've ever given a damn about.

434
00:29:49.709 --> 00:29:51.677
Cameron is so not perfect.

435
00:29:51.745 --> 00:29:53.679
Well, nobody's perfect.

436
00:29:53.747 --> 00:29:55.681
Mother Teresa?
Dead.

437
00:29:55.750 --> 00:29:57.581
Angelina Jolie?

438
00:29:57.654 --> 00:30:00.350
No medical degree.
Now who's being picky?

439
00:30:00.424 --> 00:30:02.984
You're gonna wind up alone,
House.

440
00:30:03.060 --> 00:30:05.426
You were right.
There's a significant bleed
in her temporal lobe.

441
00:30:05.498 --> 00:30:07.432
[Chase]
But no poisons.

442
00:30:07.500 --> 00:30:10.799
Did tox screens on
her blood, urine, and hair.
Nothing. Did them twice.

443
00:30:10.871 --> 00:30:13.704
He's a little dehydrated.
Put him on a saline drip
and give him some orange juice.

444
00:30:13.775 --> 00:30:17.302
I need an operating room
and a neurosurgeon.

445
00:30:17.380 --> 00:30:19.280
Given the current crisis,
I'm tempted to say no,

446
00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:21.340
but since you've been
so sweet to me today-

447
00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:23.911
Our little mermaid is bleeding
into her temporal lobe.

448
00:30:23.989 --> 00:30:27.892
- How fast can you have her prepped?
- Twenty minutes.

449
00:30:27.961 --> 00:30:30.657
You'll have a surgeon in the room in ten.

450
00:30:39.812 --> 00:30:42.645
[Muffled Conversation]

451
00:30:48.323 --> 00:30:51.486
Mr. And Mrs. Carroll?
Are you Dr. House?

452
00:30:51.561 --> 00:30:54.189
- This is Dr. Foreman.
- Is Mary all right?

453
00:30:54.265 --> 00:30:56.199
The operation went well.

454
00:30:56.268 --> 00:30:59.431
The intracranial pressure's been relieved,
and the swelling's already
going down.

455
00:30:59.505 --> 00:31:01.837
Oh, thank God.
Well, what happened?

456
00:31:01.908 --> 00:31:04.274
I mean, did she bang her head
at a meet, or did she-

457
00:31:04.346 --> 00:31:09.148
- No, nothing like that.
- Then why is she bleeding?
Is she gonna be all right?

458
00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:12.444
I'm sorry.
We still don't know.

459
00:31:35.055 --> 00:31:37.888
[Chase]
No toxins, no tumor, no bone cancer.

460
00:31:37.959 --> 00:31:40.519
[Foreman]
Renal failure could cause the rash,
fever, and muscle pain.

461
00:31:40.596 --> 00:31:43.292
Maybe it's some sort
of genetic kidney disorder.
[Chase] No family history.

462
00:31:43.366 --> 00:31:46.529
- And no blood in her urine or uremia.
- Not yet.

463
00:31:46.604 --> 00:31:49.698
You want to do a differential based
on symptoms that might happen?

464
00:31:49.775 --> 00:31:51.743
- You got a better idea?
- Stop it.

465
00:31:52.947 --> 00:31:56.508
Stop looking for things we don't know
and focus on what we do know.

466
00:31:56.585 --> 00:31:59.487
What do we actually know,
besides what's up there?

467
00:32:02.026 --> 00:32:05.427
Come on.
How hard can it be
to tell me what you already know?

468
00:32:05.497 --> 00:32:09.434
- She's 12.
- She spends a lot of time in pools-
exposure to chemicals.

469
00:32:09.503 --> 00:32:11.437
- [Chase] She travels a lot.
- But never out of the country.

470
00:32:11.506 --> 00:32:14.498
[House]
What else?

471
00:32:14.577 --> 00:32:16.977
Come on!

472
00:32:32.870 --> 00:32:34.804
We're gonna put you
right here.

473
00:32:37.074 --> 00:32:39.804
We're missing something.

474
00:32:39.878 --> 00:32:42.506
What?
Well, if I knew that,
it wouldn't be missing.

475
00:32:44.251 --> 00:32:47.311
[Chase]
Maybe she's adopted
and we've got the wrong history.

476
00:32:47.389 --> 00:32:50.688
No. She's got her mom's eyes
and a red patch of hair just like Dad.

477
00:32:50.761 --> 00:32:53.025
[Foreman]
What about an allergic reaction?

478
00:32:53.097 --> 00:32:56.864
That could explain the rash and muscle pain,
but probably not the bleeding or seizures.

479
00:32:56.935 --> 00:33:00.234
That's a lot of balloons.

480
00:33:00.307 --> 00:33:05.177
- You think she's allergic to polyester?
- Not unless she's been competing
in the nude all these years.

481
00:33:05.247 --> 00:33:09.479
Then what are you thinking?
What do the balloons mean?

482
00:33:14.126 --> 00:33:16.994
What if the rash isn't a rash?

483
00:33:17.063 --> 00:33:18.997
What are you talking about?

484
00:33:19.066 --> 00:33:22.399
Who gave her the balloons?
Some of the girls
from her team.

485
00:33:22.471 --> 00:33:25.929
They've been visiting her pretty regularly,
but none of them are sick.
What about the guys?

486
00:33:26.009 --> 00:33:28.569
- None of them are sick either.
- Which guys visited her?

487
00:33:28.646 --> 00:33:30.580
Uh-
[Sighs]

488
00:33:30.648 --> 00:33:32.706
Actually, none.

489
00:33:35.990 --> 00:33:38.356
She's cute. She's nice.

490
00:33:38.427 --> 00:33:40.918
She's a kick-ass diver.

491
00:33:40.997 --> 00:33:44.593
You'd think the guys would be
falling all over themselves
to get close to her.

492
00:33:44.668 --> 00:33:47.604
She's 12.
The youngest guy
on her team is 16.

493
00:33:47.672 --> 00:33:52.076
- Okay, so maybe they're
just not interested, or-
- They're avoiding her.

494
00:33:53.281 --> 00:33:55.215
There any cell fragments
in her blood smears?

495
00:33:57.287 --> 00:34:00.814
No. Red blood cells were intact.

496
00:34:06.799 --> 00:34:09.267
Check 'em again.

497
00:34:18.582 --> 00:34:21.574
Blood looks like it's been
put through the blender now.

498
00:34:21.653 --> 00:34:24.645
[Sighs]
You done yet?
You were right.

499
00:34:24.724 --> 00:34:28.285
The rash wasn't a rash.
She's bleeding into her skin.
It's purpura.

500
00:34:28.362 --> 00:34:30.694
Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura?

501
00:34:30.766 --> 00:34:33.326
Starts with "T."
You were so close.

502
00:34:33.403 --> 00:34:35.303
[Foreman]
What could have set it off?

503
00:34:35.372 --> 00:34:37.306
She had no traces of E. Coli in her cultures.

504
00:34:37.375 --> 00:34:39.673
She's obviously not menopausal,
so no estrogen.

505
00:34:39.745 --> 00:34:42.339
There is one other possible cause.

506
00:34:44.585 --> 00:34:46.382
Oh, God.

507
00:34:54.699 --> 00:34:56.633
Pregnancy causes...

508
00:34:56.702 --> 00:34:58.726
all kinds of chemical
and biological changes...

509
00:34:58.806 --> 00:35:00.637
in a woman's body-

510
00:35:00.707 --> 00:35:04.143
or a girl's body,
as the case may be.

511
00:35:07.216 --> 00:35:11.916
In extremely rare cases,
everything goes haywire.
It's called T.T.P.

512
00:35:11.990 --> 00:35:17.429
Blood starts clotting like crazy
and clogs the vessels
in your brain and kidneys.

513
00:35:17.498 --> 00:35:22.937
Red blood cells end up getting shredded
as they squeeze past the clot,

514
00:35:23.004 --> 00:35:24.938
like a fat guy in a crowded bar.

515
00:35:26.510 --> 00:35:29.412
I'm sure you know what that's like.

516
00:35:29.481 --> 00:35:31.676
I mean, you're only 12,
but you're all grown up, right?

517
00:35:31.751 --> 00:35:36.017
Travel on your own,
hang out in hotel rooms...

518
00:35:36.090 --> 00:35:38.786
getting room service
with your teammates.

519
00:35:38.862 --> 00:35:42.594
Maybe someone sneaks in a couple of beers.
You start playing spin the bottle.

520
00:35:42.666 --> 00:35:45.726
Next thing you know you're
waking up with nothing on but your socks.

521
00:35:45.804 --> 00:35:48.637
It wasn't like that.
Of course not.

522
00:35:48.708 --> 00:35:52.701
- You wanted it.
- Yeah. I did.

523
00:35:52.780 --> 00:35:55.271
He turned out to be a jerk, but-

524
00:35:55.351 --> 00:35:57.546
Actually, under New Jersey law,
the term is felon.

525
00:35:59.956 --> 00:36:02.322
I knew what I was doing.

526
00:36:04.163 --> 00:36:06.495
We're gonna have to do something
called plasmapheresis.

527
00:36:06.566 --> 00:36:09.126
Cleans the antibodies
from your blood.

528
00:36:09.203 --> 00:36:11.831
We're also gonna have
to terminate the pregnancy.

529
00:36:15.811 --> 00:36:17.745
You gonna tell my parents?

530
00:36:18.950 --> 00:36:22.408
Someone should.
Rock, paper, scissors?

531
00:36:22.488 --> 00:36:24.786
They don't need to know.

532
00:36:24.858 --> 00:36:27.088
I'll be all right.

533
00:36:27.161 --> 00:36:29.185
Of course you will.

534
00:36:29.264 --> 00:36:32.529
I mean, if you're old enough
to bleed out of your vagina,

535
00:36:32.603 --> 00:36:34.833
then obviously you're mature enough...

536
00:36:34.905 --> 00:36:38.637
to handle a simple thing like an abortion
without Mommy and Daddy's help.

537
00:36:43.650 --> 00:36:45.640
You gonna tell my parents?

538
00:36:49.492 --> 00:36:53.361
Under New Jersey law,
you're the boss.

539
00:36:58.071 --> 00:37:00.733
[Murmuring]

540
00:37:03.612 --> 00:37:05.546
Your daughter has T.T.P.

541
00:37:05.615 --> 00:37:08.015
Don't worry. It's curable.
She'll be fine.

542
00:37:08.085 --> 00:37:11.817
Well, wait.
I mean, what does T.T.P.
Stand for?

543
00:37:12.992 --> 00:37:14.926
Some really big words
that you've never heard before...

544
00:37:14.995 --> 00:37:16.929
and, when we're done,
will never hear again.

545
00:37:16.998 --> 00:37:18.932
Have a nice day.

546
00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:23.631
- Well, when can we take her home?
- Uh, in a few days.

547
00:37:23.706 --> 00:37:26.903
She needs some minor surgery
to remove the underlying cause...

548
00:37:26.978 --> 00:37:30.881
before we can do the...
another really big word.

549
00:37:30.950 --> 00:37:33.418
What's the underlying cause?

550
00:37:34.889 --> 00:37:38.950
- She has an abnormal growth
in her abdomen.
- What kind of surgery?

551
00:37:39.028 --> 00:37:40.996
It's-
It's very simple.

552
00:37:41.064 --> 00:37:43.362
We do it here all the time.

553
00:37:43.434 --> 00:37:46.699
- Could you be a little more specific?
- Actually, no.

554
00:37:47.840 --> 00:37:50.240
I'm sorry.

555
00:38:02.027 --> 00:38:04.359
[Woman Murmuring]

556
00:38:16.112 --> 00:38:18.046
We're almost done.

557
00:38:21.086 --> 00:38:23.020
Hang in there.

558
00:38:30.032 --> 00:38:31.966
You're doing good.

559
00:38:33.169 --> 00:38:35.103
Feeling okay?

560
00:38:35.172 --> 00:38:37.106
Yeah.
You should be.

561
00:38:37.175 --> 00:38:39.973
- Your platelets count's up.
- How's your neck?

562
00:38:43.083 --> 00:38:45.881
Looks good.
Anything else we can get you?

563
00:38:45.954 --> 00:38:48.445
No, thanks.

564
00:38:48.525 --> 00:38:50.891
Okay.

565
00:38:52.363 --> 00:38:55.491
Yeah.

566
00:38:57.203 --> 00:38:59.398
Can I see my mom and dad?

567
00:39:17.398 --> 00:39:20.731
[No Audible Dialogue]

568
00:39:30.983 --> 00:39:33.349
Plasmapheresis is working.
She's gonna be fine.

569
00:39:34.422 --> 00:39:36.356
I know.

570
00:39:49.676 --> 00:39:51.610
Hi.
I've got these.

571
00:39:51.679 --> 00:39:54.045
[Indistinct Conversations]

572
00:40:09.971 --> 00:40:12.063
I can't even tell you
how much I appreciate...

573
00:40:12.140 --> 00:40:14.802
the opportunity to meet with you.

574
00:40:17.681 --> 00:40:21.947
- The moment I heard
you had another fellowship opening, l-
- There is no opening.

575
00:40:23.190 --> 00:40:25.090
House.

576
00:40:25.159 --> 00:40:28.027
- You have to hire someone.
- I know.

577
00:40:29.331 --> 00:40:31.355
Position's been filled.

578
00:40:33.938 --> 00:40:37.430
- Why am I interviewing for a position
that's already been filled?
- Exactly.

579
00:40:41.347 --> 00:40:43.315
I called to confirm the interview
this morning.

580
00:40:43.384 --> 00:40:46.286
You figure if you keep arguing,
I'm gonna cave,

581
00:40:46.354 --> 00:40:48.288
admit it's all a lie and hire you?

582
00:40:55.301 --> 00:40:58.532
Do you need your parking validated?

583
00:40:58.605 --> 00:41:01.096
[Cane Rapping]

584
00:41:03.312 --> 00:41:07.113
[Rapping]

585
00:41:13.994 --> 00:41:15.928
I don't wanna interview anyone else.

586
00:41:15.997 --> 00:41:17.931
You're interviewing?

587
00:41:17.999 --> 00:41:21.025
I thought you'd just have them
send a head shot
along with their C.V.

588
00:41:21.104 --> 00:41:24.040
Ha.

589
00:41:24.107 --> 00:41:27.599
That's good,
and why I need you around-

590
00:41:27.679 --> 00:41:29.840
to keep me in my place.

591
00:41:29.916 --> 00:41:32.578
I can't come back.
I told you that.

592
00:41:32.653 --> 00:41:35.213
- Wasn't listening.
- Right.

593
00:41:36.692 --> 00:41:39.525
You want me to listen to you more?
I can do that.

594
00:41:40.530 --> 00:41:42.464
Right.

595
00:41:42.533 --> 00:41:44.625
I already accepted a position
somewhere else.

596
00:41:46.372 --> 00:41:50.207
- With who?
- Yeuell- atJefferson.

597
00:41:50.277 --> 00:41:53.303
- Unaccept it.
- Why?

598
00:41:56.319 --> 00:41:58.913
Because Yeuell is boring.

599
00:41:58.989 --> 00:42:01.925
He's pedantic and preachy.

600
00:42:01.993 --> 00:42:05.623
Because he's short.

601
00:42:06.701 --> 00:42:08.965
Because I want you to come back.

602
00:42:12.841 --> 00:42:15.435
Not good enough.

603
00:42:18.684 --> 00:42:21.983
Want more money?
A car allowance?

604
00:42:22.055 --> 00:42:24.683
Better parking space?

605
00:42:27.195 --> 00:42:29.163
Dinner.

606
00:42:32.169 --> 00:42:34.967
And not just a meal
between two colleagues.

607
00:42:35.039 --> 00:42:37.337
A date.

608
00:42:46.322 --> 00:42:49.416
You'll come back to work...

609
00:42:49.493 --> 00:42:52.018
if I go out on a date with you?

610
00:42:52.097 --> 00:42:54.497
Yes.

611
00:42:58.672 --> 00:43:01.232
Okay.

612
00:43:01.310 --> 00:43:03.244
It's a deal.

613
00:43:11.690 --> 00:43:13.680
See you tomorrow morning.

614
00:43:15.497 --> 00:43:17.431
Don't be late.

615
00:43:17.500 --> 00:43:19.434
I won't.

616
00:44:01.526 --> 00:44:02.787
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>

